What was adapted
----------------

The following parts of "Локальный инференс LLM" draw on ideas, formulas,
classifications, or the order of analysis from the works above. The text was
not copied verbatim: it was paraphrased, re-scoped to single-machine local
inference (one PC, Mac, mini-PC; llama.cpp and MLX), and supplemented with
new examples, calculations, and cross-references to this book's chapters.

  * fallacies.md — the symptom-indexed catalogue of misconceptions. Its
    structure and several entries are adapted from references/fallacies.md
    in the Designing AI Infra skill and from the "Заблуждения и ловушки"
    sections of AI Infra in Depth (chapters 1–5 and 8). New entries
    address local-scale issues: GB vs GiB, context vs weights, memory
    bandwidth vs TFLOPS, quantization overhead, and speculative decoding.
  * cheatsheet.md — the analysis order, the "five overlooked constraints",
    and the question → formula → chapter table. Adapted from
    references/cheatsheet.md and the preface of AI Infra in Depth.
  * 12-benchmark-methodology.md, §12.7 — "измерение против нижней границы":
    lower-bound calculation, MBU/MFU, decomposition into queue / prefill /
    decode / steps, and the one-hypothesis-one-condition rule. Adapted from
    references/playbooks/diagnose-serving.md and from chapters 1 and 8 of
    AI Infra in Depth.
  * 02-prefill-decode-roofline.md, §2.8 — TTFT and ITL as separate metrics.
    Adapted from chapter 8, §8.1.3 of AI Infra in Depth.
  * 08-batching-vllm.md — Little's law for the request queue and the batch
    threshold b* where KV reads overtake weight reads. Adapted from
    chapters 3 and 8 of AI Infra in Depth.
  * 09-speculative-decoding.md, §9.3 — the expected accepted-chain length
    E[N] and the break-even draft budget. Adapted from chapter 8, §8.5.2
    of AI Infra in Depth; consistent with Leviathan et al. (2022).
  * 15-where-to-go-next.md, §15.2 — the "next level: from one PC to a
    cluster and training" reading route. Based on the structure of
    AI Infra in Depth (chapters 1–12).
  * 16-glossary.md — definitions of lower bound, MBU/MFU, effective
    throughput, Little's law, b*, E[N], and break-even draft.
  * sources.md — bibliographic entries for the original book, the Russian
    community translation, and the Designing AI Infra skill.

